    "theorem_summary": "The nonsquarefree defect locus of Phi3(q)=q^2+q+1 and Phi6(q)=q^2-q+1 is exactly the union over split primes p congruent to 1 mod 3 of the two Hensel-lifted nontrivial cube roots of unity modulo p^2, with the Phi6 classes given by their negatives. Equivalently, Phi3(q)=N(q-omega) and Phi6(q)=N(q+omega) in the Eisenstein integers, so the defect set is the split-prime multiplicity locus of those two norm packets."
